// U7 L2 Quiz

::U7 L2 Quiz Q01::Neighborhood B has a higher asthma-visit rate and more traffic. What may be concluded? {=There is a pattern worth investigating, but the data alone do not prove traffic caused it.~Traffic definitely caused every visit.~The neighborhoods are identical.~Rates cannot be compared.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q02::Why use a rate rather than a raw count? {=A rate accounts for population size or time and permits fairer comparison.~A rate always proves causation.~Raw counts are never useful.~Rates remove all bias.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q03::Which is a community health determinant? {=Reliable transportation to health services.~A person’s favorite color.~The title of a survey.~A random password.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q04::A park plan improves access but removes a bus stop. What should planners examine? {=Unintended effects on people who depend on transit.~Only the opening-day attendance.~Whether the plan has a catchy name.~Only the construction color.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q05::Which action best supports an equity analysis? {=Compare who benefits, who bears burdens, and who faces access barriers.~Assume one solution affects everyone equally.~Exclude affected residents from planning.~Use averages only.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q06::Air readings were collected on one calm morning. What is a key limitation? {=One time point may not represent typical or peak exposure.~Air cannot be measured.~Morning data are automatically false.~Location never matters.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q07::What best distinguishes correlation from causation? {=Correlation shows variables move together; causation requires evidence that one produces change in the other.~Correlation is stronger than experimental evidence.~They mean exactly the same thing.~Causation requires no mechanism.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q08::Which measure best evaluates a new safe-routes program? {=Changes in route use and injury/near-miss data over a defined period.~The logo color.~One organizer’s opinion only.~Total city population.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q09::Why include residents’ perspectives with quantitative data? {=Experiences can reveal barriers and context that counts alone miss.~Stories automatically prove cause.~Numbers should always be ignored.~Perspective eliminates sampling concerns.}

::U7 L2 Quiz Q10::Which response is most proportionate to uncertain evidence? {=Pilot a low-risk action, monitor indicators, and revise using results.~Make an irreversible change immediately.~Take no action under any uncertainty.~Hide the uncertainty.}

